      it to the Service;

  (b) use the Software, including its source code, to develop, test,
      document or operate a collector, backend or service that receives
      Telemetry from the Software, or that substitutes for the Service;

  (c) remove, disable or circumvent any part of the Software that limits
      where it sends Telemetry; or

  (d) remove or obscure any licensing, copyright or trademark notice in the
      Software.

Exporting Telemetry through an export option included in a version of the
Software the Licensor released, such as OpenTelemetry (OTLP) export, as
documented for that version, does not violate (a).

Passing trace context, such as traceparent or x-request-id headers, between
Your applications and the services they call does not violate (a) or (b).

A collector used solely to test the Software or Your applications, that does
not store, display or provide monitoring of Telemetry for anyone, does not
violate (a) or (b).

